<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mariamne I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 29 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mariamne I was a Hasmonean princess, granddaughter of both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristobulus-ii">Aristobulus II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyrcanus-ii">Hyrcanus II</a>, and the second wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a>, whose claim to rule she strengthened. Suspicious of her and her family, Herod had her executed in 29 BCE, and later also had their sons Alexander and Aristobulus put to death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariamne-i.jpg" alt="Mariamne I" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Reverdy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mariamne_I_medal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
